  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The empirical validation and energy-saving rates are based on data from a single transit system, the Wuxi Metro.",
      "what": "This study formulates a coupled optimal control problem that integrates train control with underground metro vertical alignment (UMVA) using Pontryagin's Maximum Principle to derive six optimal control structures. Using real-world data from the Wuxi Metro, the researchers developed a mixed-integer quadratic programming model to calculate the ideal vertical alignment and corresponding train control strategies.",
      "why": "It quantifies the theoretical upper limit of energy savings from vertical alignment optimization, showing that while an ideal unconstrained alignment can reduce energy consumption by up to 42.05%, real-world engineering constraints reduce this maximum energy-saving rate to 27.08%."
    }
